#	Normalise text to LF in the repository and the working tree.
#
#	Biome enforces `lineEnding: "lf"`, and this project's contributors run
#	EverQuest, which means Windows. Without this, a checkout with the default
#	`core.autocrlf=true` gets CRLF everywhere and `npm run lint` reports every
#	file as malformed before the contributor has changed anything. It has already
#	happened once: a test file arrived with 131 CRLF line endings and failed the
#	format check on contact.
* text=auto eol=lf

#	Captured EverQuest logs, left exactly as the game wrote them. EverQuest logs
#	CRLF on Windows, which is what the parser tails in production, so normalising
#	these would make the sample less faithful than the real input. Nothing reads
#	them at test time; they are reference data.
#	(For the record, `tail` splits on /[\r]{0,1}\n/, so CRLF input parses fine.)
src/exampleLogs/** -text

#	Binary, so git never tries to normalise them
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
